1
00:00:19,383 --> 00:00:21,693
Did you and Ji Won have feelings for each other?

2
00:00:21,793 --> 00:00:22,853
What?

3
00:00:26,563 --> 00:00:29,562
(A man and a woman...)

4
00:00:29,563 --> 00:00:33,863
(meeting again after a long time)

5
00:00:38,303 --> 00:00:40,773
I was too young back then.

6
00:00:41,413 --> 00:00:42,573
It's been 20 years.

7
00:00:43,143 --> 00:00:45,243
No, it's been over 20 years.

8
00:00:46,143 --> 00:00:49,182
I got emotional somehow.

9
00:00:49,183 --> 00:00:50,313
I was so happy.

10
00:00:53,453 --> 00:00:55,623
She's even more beautiful than I remember.

11
00:00:56,293 --> 00:00:58,793
It's our first time appearing on a show together...

12
00:00:59,063 --> 00:01:00,663
since the drama.

13
00:01:01,563 --> 00:01:03,733
It's been 23 years.

14
00:01:04,733 --> 00:01:06,863
Actually, I was very excited...

15
00:01:07,203 --> 00:01:08,372
about...

16
00:01:08,373 --> 00:01:10,033
getting to film...

17
00:01:10,273 --> 00:01:12,743
and work together.

18
00:01:12,843 --> 00:01:15,572
I was looking forward to it.

19
00:01:15,573 --> 00:01:18,213
(23 years ago)

20
00:01:18,913 --> 00:01:20,712
("Damo" is a historical martial arts romance drama that aired in 2003,)

21
00:01:20,713 --> 00:01:22,513
(following the story of a damo, a female investigator in Joseon.)

22
00:01:22,553 --> 00:01:25,553
(25-year-old Ji Won and 32-year-old Seo Jin starred in the drama.)

23
00:01:26,483 --> 00:01:29,422
(They portrayed a romance between an officer and a damo...)

24
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:31,393
(that transcended social class.)

25
00:01:32,223 --> 00:01:38,033
(Their heartbreaking love story was so captivating...)

26
00:01:38,763 --> 00:01:41,302
(that it gave rise to a new kind of drama fan in Korea,)

27
00:01:41,303 --> 00:01:42,872
(known as "Damo Addicts.")

28
00:01:42,873 --> 00:01:45,142
("Insane! The Legendary MBC Drama 'Damo' Hits a 24.2 Percent Rating")

29
00:01:45,143 --> 00:01:47,103
("The Intense Romance Turns Viewers into 'Damo' Addicts")

30
00:01:47,303 --> 00:01:49,013
(And...)

31
00:01:49,113 --> 00:01:50,272
Does it hurt?

32
00:01:50,273 --> 00:01:52,582
(Does it hurt?)

33
00:01:52,583 --> 00:01:53,743
Yes.

34
00:01:56,483 --> 00:01:57,853
It hurts me too.

35
00:01:58,823 --> 00:02:02,723
(Even 23 years later, these lines are still iconic.)

36
00:02:04,093 --> 00:02:05,992
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

37
00:02:05,993 --> 00:02:07,322
- We've been wanting to invite you.
- Since Season One.

38
00:02:07,323 --> 00:02:08,793
(The star we've finally got after 2 years of trying since Season 1)

39
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:10,592
Thank you for having me.

40
00:02:10,593 --> 00:02:12,162
(My Star Ha Ji Won)

41
00:02:12,163 --> 00:02:13,362
(As soon as the preview was released)

42
00:02:13,363 --> 00:02:14,732
(This is why you should live a long life.)

43
00:02:14,733 --> 00:02:16,232
(Who would've thought we'd get to see these two together again?)

44
00:02:16,233 --> 00:02:21,473
(The "Damo" addicts got super excited.)

45
00:02:21,713 --> 00:02:24,342
(It feels like they were reincarnated...)

46
00:02:24,343 --> 00:02:26,183
(and reunited in the modern world.)

47
00:02:26,943 --> 00:02:29,553
(The couple was reincarnated 23 years later.)

48
00:02:30,383 --> 00:02:31,952
(They're not heartbroken anymore.)

49
00:02:31,953 --> 00:02:34,153
(They laugh whenever they're together.)

50
00:02:34,723 --> 00:02:37,023
(Are you having fun? I'm having fun too.)

51
00:02:37,593 --> 00:02:41,563
(You guys are going to make "Damo" Season 2.)

52
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:45,202
(A love left unfulfilled 23 years ago)

53
00:02:45,203 --> 00:02:48,903
(Will things be different this time?)

54
00:02:50,603 --> 00:02:56,073
(The 2026 reunion will make "Damo" addicts' hearts skip a beat.)

55
00:02:56,473 --> 00:02:57,713
But you're originally tanned.

56
00:02:59,313 --> 00:03:02,883
(Incheon International Airport at 1:30pm)

57
00:03:03,313 --> 00:03:05,923
(Seo Jin has never been this early before.)

58
00:03:06,183 --> 00:03:07,852
- Are we not meeting Ji Won here?
- We are.

59
00:03:07,853 --> 00:03:08,922
Here?

60
00:03:08,923 --> 00:03:11,193
(He looks for My Star as soon as he gets here.)

61
00:03:11,593 --> 00:03:13,393
- You came quickly.
- Sorry?

62
00:03:15,233 --> 00:03:16,863
You told me to come even earlier than this.

63
00:03:17,663 --> 00:03:19,163
Why did you tell me to come so early?

64
00:03:19,363 --> 00:03:21,063
- We wanted to film you.
- What?

65
00:03:21,373 --> 00:03:22,872
Why would you want to shoot here?

66
00:03:22,873 --> 00:03:24,603
- It's so chaotic.
- It's because...

67
00:03:25,903 --> 00:03:27,242
There aren't many people.

68
00:03:27,243 --> 00:03:28,542
(Looking around)

69
00:03:28,543 --> 00:03:29,812
There aren't a lot of people here.

70
00:03:29,813 --> 00:03:32,513
(He talks to himself. He definitely looks excited.)

71
00:03:33,113 --> 00:03:34,913
(When is Ji Won coming?)

72
00:03:36,653 --> 00:03:37,752
Hello.

73
00:03:37,753 --> 00:03:39,323
(His older bestie came to work.)

74
00:03:39,783 --> 00:03:42,092
(Instantly disappointed)

75
00:03:42,093 --> 00:03:43,122
Hello.

76
00:03:43,123 --> 00:03:45,763
You're flying business class. Why would you bring a neck pillow?

77
00:03:46,463 --> 00:03:47,723
Are we flying business class?

78
00:03:48,063 --> 00:03:49,162
You fly economy class then.

79
00:03:49,163 --> 00:03:50,233
Are we?

80
00:03:50,333 --> 00:03:52,963
There are already so many articles about it.

81
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,033
- About what?
- Have you seen them?

82
00:03:55,173 --> 00:03:57,673
- What article?
- Haven't you seen them?

83
00:03:57,773 --> 00:03:59,042
Articles about Ji Won appearing on our show?

84
00:03:59,043 --> 00:04:01,102
("Lee Seo Jin and Ha Ji Won Reunites on My Genie Secretary")

85
00:04:01,103 --> 00:04:02,313
About your reunion.

86
00:04:02,343 --> 00:04:04,473
People are looking forward to it.

87
00:04:05,913 --> 00:04:07,913
Actually, I've never...

88
00:04:08,313 --> 00:04:10,583
been on a show with Ji Won.

89
00:04:11,323 --> 00:04:12,422
(Seo Jin has been looking forward to reuniting with her after 23 years.)

90
00:04:12,423 --> 00:04:13,853
- Since "Damo?"
- Yes.

91
00:04:14,423 --> 00:04:16,422
First time appearing on a show together since "Damo?"

92
00:04:16,423 --> 00:04:17,992
- It's our first time.
- Unbelievable.

93
00:04:17,993 --> 00:04:19,063
Ji Won...

94
00:04:20,493 --> 00:04:21,963
looks even more beautiful now than before.

95
00:04:22,863 --> 00:04:24,563
She's gotten so much prettier.

96
00:04:25,633 --> 00:04:27,003
She looks like a different person now.

97
00:04:27,563 --> 00:04:28,873
Are you saying she wasn't pretty back then?

98
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:30,573
Back then, she was just...

99
00:04:31,403 --> 00:04:34,443
(He tends to tease people when he's really happy to see them.)

100
00:04:35,013 --> 00:04:36,573
Anyway, she's a lot more beautiful now.

101
00:04:37,213 --> 00:04:38,513
Last night,

102
00:04:39,343 --> 00:04:41,182
I was flipping through the channels, and "Damo" came on.

103
00:04:41,183 --> 00:04:43,282
- Really?
- What?

104
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:45,682
It was Episode 11 or 12.

105
00:04:45,683 --> 00:04:46,823
(He revisited his memories with My Star.)

106
00:04:47,153 --> 00:04:48,823
Someone commented,

107
00:04:49,123 --> 00:04:52,462
- "She used to serve Mr. Officer,"
- Yes.

108
00:04:52,463 --> 00:04:53,593
"but now the tables have turned."

109
00:04:53,663 --> 00:04:56,293
Right. She was my servant back then.

110
00:04:56,763 --> 00:04:57,893
She was my servant.

111
00:04:58,033 --> 00:04:59,963
- Your roles have been reversed.
- Yes.

112
00:05:01,163 --> 00:05:02,373
It was about time.

113
00:05:04,133 --> 00:05:06,403
- She hasn't arrived yet, right?
- She's almost here.

114
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:10,813
(Right then,)

115
00:05:12,283 --> 00:05:15,983
(the person Seo Jin has been waiting for has arrived.)

116
00:05:18,953 --> 00:05:21,793
(Seo Jin keeps glancing at the entrance.)

117
00:05:22,793 --> 00:05:27,793
(She's going to meet the officer now.)

118
00:05:28,533 --> 00:05:30,232
- Can I go to the restroom?
- The restroom?

119
00:05:30,233 --> 00:05:31,563
- Yes.
- Later.

120
00:05:31,803 --> 00:05:32,832
The restroom is over there.

121
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:33,902
(He wants to use the restroom. He's probably nervous.)

122
00:05:33,903 --> 00:05:35,133
I think she's here.

123
00:05:36,303 --> 00:05:37,932
- She's here?
- I think so.

124
00:05:37,933 --> 00:05:39,103
Did she walk into the airport?

125
00:05:40,043 --> 00:05:41,072
Is she here?

126
00:05:41,073 --> 00:05:42,573
(My Star is walking toward them from a distance.)

127
00:05:44,313 --> 00:05:47,583
(She's here.)

128
00:05:47,883 --> 00:05:51,083
(3 seconds before meeting My Star)

129
00:05:53,623 --> 00:05:54,823
- Seo Jin.
- Ji Won.

130
00:05:55,123 --> 00:05:56,593
- Hey.
- Gosh.

131
00:05:58,423 --> 00:06:01,433
(Seo Jin!)

132
00:06:03,793 --> 00:06:06,703
(Ji Won!)

133
00:06:06,963 --> 00:06:08,002
I was going to use the restroom.

134
00:06:08,003 --> 00:06:09,003
- Seo Jin.
- Ji Won.

135
00:06:09,004 --> 00:06:11,372
(The damo and the officer...)

136
00:06:11,373 --> 00:06:14,273
(finally reunite.)

137
00:06:14,673 --> 00:06:17,673
(It's been a while since we've seen his dimples show up this deeply.)

138
00:06:21,513 --> 00:06:22,912
Hello, Kwang Kyu.

139
00:06:22,913 --> 00:06:25,053
You don't have to bow so politely. He's your secretary.

140
00:06:25,353 --> 00:06:26,652
Give me a hug too.

141
00:06:26,653 --> 00:06:27,682
(My Star and Kwang Kyu were in the same drama too.)

142
00:06:27,683 --> 00:06:29,653
- It's been a long time.
- It's been a long time.

143
00:06:30,623 --> 00:06:32,393
Ji Won has gotten so much more beautiful, right?

144
00:06:32,623 --> 00:06:34,323
Ji Won has gotten so much more beautiful, right?

145
00:06:34,563 --> 00:06:35,893
- Why would you say that?
- She...

146
00:06:36,033 --> 00:06:37,862
I mean it. She's so beautiful these days.

147
00:06:37,863 --> 00:06:40,302
He kept saying you've gotten more beautiful.

148
00:06:40,303 --> 00:06:43,372
- She wasn't this pretty back then.
- He was praising you...

149
00:06:43,373 --> 00:06:45,872
- Come on.
- He said you've gotten so pretty.

150
00:06:45,873 --> 00:06:47,743
- That's true. You look...
- Really?

151
00:06:47,803 --> 00:06:48,873
better than ever.

152
00:06:48,973 --> 00:06:51,613
(He says she wasn't so pretty back then,)

153
00:06:52,113 --> 00:06:55,813
(but Mr. Officer gazed at her lovingly.)

154
00:06:55,953 --> 00:06:57,082
You look better than ever.

155
00:06:57,083 --> 00:06:58,583
- Really?
- I was surprised at the hair salon.

156
00:06:58,783 --> 00:07:01,282
I guess going to college has made her look younger.

157
00:07:01,283 --> 00:07:02,922
- It's the youthful energy.
- Yes.

158
00:07:02,923 --> 00:07:04,963
I think going to college has made her look younger.

159
00:07:05,093 --> 00:07:06,162
Right.

160
00:07:06,163 --> 00:07:07,823
- Have a seat.
- Do you want me to sit?

161
00:07:08,563 --> 00:07:09,732
My gosh.

162
00:07:09,733 --> 00:07:11,503
(Feeling shy for no reason)

163
00:07:12,863 --> 00:07:13,902
- This is nice.
- Seo Jin.

164
00:07:13,903 --> 00:07:15,402
Seo Jin, didn't you want to go to the restroom?

165
00:07:15,403 --> 00:07:17,433
- Can you wait a little bit?
- Yes.

166
00:07:17,503 --> 00:07:18,972
(I'm not going to the restroom when My Star is here.)

167
00:07:18,973 --> 00:07:21,173
- Later then?
- Yes.

168
00:07:21,513 --> 00:07:23,143
- Hello.
- What are those?

169
00:07:23,543 --> 00:07:24,943
Do you carry around those things?

170
00:07:24,983 --> 00:07:27,612
Hello, I'm Ji Won's manager.

171
00:07:27,613 --> 00:07:29,383
- Oh, my.
- You're her manager.

172
00:07:29,813 --> 00:07:31,622
Okay. This is the schedule.

173
00:07:31,623 --> 00:07:32,822
(What is her overseas schedule?)

174
00:07:32,823 --> 00:07:36,553
This time, Ji Won...

175
00:07:37,193 --> 00:07:39,462
has been invited by the Singapore Tourism Board...

176
00:07:39,463 --> 00:07:42,833
to attend the Grand Prix for the first time.

177
00:07:43,193 --> 00:07:45,602
On the first day, she'll be attending the F1 race.

178
00:07:45,603 --> 00:07:48,202
Since this is a special invitation,

179
00:07:48,203 --> 00:07:49,832
I'd appreciate it if you could take good care of her.

180
00:07:49,833 --> 00:07:51,073
(My Star was invited to an F1 event?)

181
00:07:56,373 --> 00:07:59,682
(F1 is the world's premier motorsport competition,)

182
00:07:59,683 --> 00:08:02,553
(organized by the Federation Internationale de I'Automobile.)

183
00:08:03,213 --> 00:08:04,882
(Races can be decided by thousandths of a second,)

184
00:08:04,883 --> 00:08:06,553
(with cars reaching speeds of over 370km per hour.)

185
00:08:07,883 --> 00:08:10,152
(Each car costs more than 10 million dollars.)

186
00:08:10,153 --> 00:08:14,763
(It's one of the biggest racing competitions on the planet.)

187
00:08:15,193 --> 00:08:20,463
(A global sport watched by 800 million people around the world)

188
00:08:20,803 --> 00:08:23,173
(From global star Kim Kardashian...)

189
00:08:23,233 --> 00:08:24,672
(to Jang Won Young, CORTIS, and Jung Hae In,)

190
00:08:24,673 --> 00:08:26,003
(it's a major international event that attracts celebrities.)

191
00:08:26,143 --> 00:08:27,202
("Ha Ji Won Receives VIP Treatment in Singapore")

192
00:08:27,203 --> 00:08:28,812
(My Star, who helped lead...)

193
00:08:28,813 --> 00:08:30,443
(the Korean Wave through her fan meetings,)

194
00:08:30,913 --> 00:08:32,612
(was invited by the Singapore Tourism Board...)

195
00:08:32,613 --> 00:08:34,283
(for the chance to watch the F1 Grand Prix live.)

196
00:08:36,383 --> 00:08:38,422
(Thanks to My Star,)

197
00:08:38,423 --> 00:08:40,483
(the secretaries also got to watch the F1 race.)

198
00:08:41,523 --> 00:08:43,593
(The world of F1 right before their eyes)

199
00:08:44,053 --> 00:08:46,663
(And...)

200
00:08:47,993 --> 00:08:50,863
(This is the most special place!)

201
00:08:50,993 --> 00:08:53,703
(They were given access to a place few people get to visit?)

202
00:08:54,203 --> 00:08:56,433
(The sound is different!)

203
00:08:57,133 --> 00:09:01,202
(We're about to reveal exclusive footage...)

204
00:09:01,203 --> 00:09:03,573
(of an F1 race experience, for the 1st time in Korea.)

205
00:09:07,283 --> 00:09:10,883
(Why was My Star invited to an F1 event?)

206
00:09:11,723 --> 00:09:14,783
I'm a fan of F1.

207
00:09:15,023 --> 00:09:16,323
- Really?
- Yes.

208
00:09:16,823 --> 00:09:18,863
- You were into racing? Since when?
- Yes.

209
00:09:19,823 --> 00:09:21,293
Since 2024.

210
00:09:22,463 --> 00:09:25,333
- I think that's just how I'm wired.
- Right.

211
00:09:26,663 --> 00:09:29,233
It's a sport...

212
00:09:29,803 --> 00:09:31,373
where you could lose your life,

213
00:09:31,673 --> 00:09:33,443
yet the drivers throw themselves into it.

214
00:09:33,903 --> 00:09:35,243
I have so much respect for that.

215
00:09:36,713 --> 00:09:38,442
Really?

216
00:09:38,443 --> 00:09:40,183
- Yes.
- You don't even drive, do you?

217
00:09:40,713 --> 00:09:42,483
- How did you know?
- Seriously.

218
00:09:42,613 --> 00:09:44,783
You don't even drive. How come you like F1?

219
00:09:45,053 --> 00:09:47,223
(They giggle over nothing.)

220
00:09:47,483 --> 00:09:50,693
She's quite sensitive when it comes to food.

221
00:09:51,293 --> 00:09:53,262
Is she a picky eater?

222
00:09:53,263 --> 00:09:54,792
- She used to eat anything.
- Yes.

223
00:09:54,793 --> 00:09:56,433
Why would you say that?

224
00:09:56,893 --> 00:09:59,232
- You used to eat anything.
- No.

225
00:09:59,233 --> 00:10:00,332
You've changed a lot.

226
00:10:00,333 --> 00:10:01,533
- So she...
- "You've changed a lot."

227
00:10:01,933 --> 00:10:03,772
- We've met again just now.
- She's...

228
00:10:03,773 --> 00:10:06,542
the most easygoing actress I know. She's not picky about food at all.

229
00:10:06,543 --> 00:10:08,143
- That's not true.
- You always...

230
00:10:08,543 --> 00:10:10,213
- You weren't picky. Am I?
- You're mistaken.

231
00:10:10,473 --> 00:10:12,212
- You weren't a picky eater.
- That's not true.

232
00:10:12,213 --> 00:10:13,513
(He tried to act like he knew, but failed.)

233
00:10:15,353 --> 00:10:18,423
It says you often lose your stuff. Is it right?

234
00:10:19,453 --> 00:10:21,653
- These are all her belongings.
- Okay.

235
00:10:21,853 --> 00:10:25,023
If you let her carry them, she'll likely lose them.

236
00:10:25,293 --> 00:10:28,263
- Is that so?
- So you should carry these.

237
00:10:28,663 --> 00:10:30,762
- During a shoot...
- I often leave my things behind.

238
00:10:30,763 --> 00:10:31,763
(My Star is quite clumsy.)

239
00:10:32,463 --> 00:10:34,303
Give this to her...

240
00:10:34,603 --> 00:10:35,972
- when she gets in the car.
- Hey.

241
00:10:35,973 --> 00:10:37,932
Is she in kindergarten or something? Does she really carry this around?

242
00:10:37,933 --> 00:10:39,442
- What's this for?
- What's this for?

243
00:10:39,443 --> 00:10:41,102
When she gets her hair and makeup done...

244
00:10:41,103 --> 00:10:42,343
- What's this for?
- What's this for?

245
00:10:42,473 --> 00:10:43,712
(Staring)

246
00:10:43,713 --> 00:10:45,983
Is this a voodoo doll?

247
00:10:46,543 --> 00:10:48,113
- I mean...
- Hey.

248
00:10:48,553 --> 00:10:51,753
People stick needles in a doll like this to curse someone.

249
00:10:52,023 --> 00:10:54,052
- The one Huibin Jang used.
- Yes.

250
00:10:54,053 --> 00:10:55,123
Seo Jin.

251
00:10:55,593 --> 00:10:56,593
It looks similar.

252
00:10:56,823 --> 00:10:58,122
- Hey.
- No.

253
00:10:58,123 --> 00:10:59,863
It's so cute.

254
00:11:00,563 --> 00:11:03,563
And this is her priority immigration card,

255
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:06,302
- The priority immigration card.
- which she received as an award.

256
00:11:06,303 --> 00:11:08,432
It's awarded to exemplary taxpayers.

257
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:10,573
She can use it to access the fast-track lane.

258
00:11:11,433 --> 00:11:13,643
("Ha Ji Won Named Exemplary Taxpayer for the Second Time")

259
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:14,772
(She's an icon of tax compliance,)

260
00:11:14,773 --> 00:11:16,413
(having been recognized by the government twice.)

261
00:11:16,613 --> 00:11:19,543
(Seo Jin has received the same award too.)

262
00:11:19,613 --> 00:11:20,613
Back then, this only allowed one more person...

263
00:11:20,613 --> 00:11:21,613
- to use the fast-track lane.
- Really?

264
00:11:21,753 --> 00:11:22,753
- Really?
- Now, it's three people.

265
00:11:22,754 --> 00:11:24,882
- Three people, including me?
- So we can just walk in?

266
00:11:24,883 --> 00:11:26,752
- Yes.
- It's quicker.

267
00:11:26,753 --> 00:11:28,183
This is the most important.

268
00:11:28,393 --> 00:11:30,853
- She should carry her passport.
- Yes.

269
00:11:31,453 --> 00:11:33,563
I'd be so nervous carrying my passport around.

270
00:11:35,023 --> 00:11:36,162
(Laughing)

271
00:11:36,163 --> 00:11:37,732
- Not the passport.
- Really?

272
00:11:37,733 --> 00:11:38,833
Give it to me. I'll keep it then.

273
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:42,903
(He teases her, then suddenly turns sweet.)

274
00:11:43,303 --> 00:11:45,873
You keep this too.

275
00:11:47,073 --> 00:11:49,242
(He's all smiles, even with her passport and plushie in his hands.)

276
00:11:49,243 --> 00:11:50,642
(Lovey-dovey)

277
00:11:50,643 --> 00:11:53,083
And I got extra clothes for her...

278
00:11:53,943 --> 00:11:55,982
- because she might get cold...
- Okay.

279
00:11:55,983 --> 00:11:57,012
on the plane.

280
00:11:57,013 --> 00:11:59,823
This is soap for the time when she uses the restroom.

281
00:12:00,183 --> 00:12:02,353
These are comfortable shoes she can change into.

282
00:12:02,653 --> 00:12:04,592
This is a portable electric fan.

283
00:12:04,593 --> 00:12:05,762
(A portable electric fan, clothes, shoes, and soap)

284
00:12:05,763 --> 00:12:07,923
You've been going through a lot.

285
00:12:08,893 --> 00:12:10,093
This is a brush...

286
00:12:11,063 --> 00:12:12,163
for her hair.

287
00:12:12,303 --> 00:12:14,733
- Is that for a dog? No?
- Gosh.

288
00:12:15,203 --> 00:12:17,632
- Gosh.
- Yes. This is for cats.

289
00:12:17,633 --> 00:12:18,902
(It's fun to tease My Star.)

290
00:12:18,903 --> 00:12:20,572
It feels so good.

291
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:22,073
That's an important bag.

292
00:12:22,613 --> 00:12:25,072
What's inside this bag? Is it empty?

293
00:12:25,073 --> 00:12:28,113
No. There's a phone...

294
00:12:28,883 --> 00:12:30,083
and a mini pouch.

295
00:12:31,153 --> 00:12:32,453
It's packed with stuff.

296
00:12:33,223 --> 00:12:36,722
You should carry this bag around for me.

297
00:12:36,723 --> 00:12:38,293
- Me?
- Yes.

298
00:12:38,393 --> 00:12:41,592
Because I build arm muscles...

299
00:12:41,593 --> 00:12:43,063
just by carrying a bag.

300
00:12:43,733 --> 00:12:44,832
(My Star is naturally muscular.)

301
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:46,533
- If you lose your muscle...
- I can't carry a bag.

302
00:12:48,003 --> 00:12:50,672
When I play certain characters, I need to have less muscle.

303
00:12:50,673 --> 00:12:52,743
That's the kind of role I recently took on.

304
00:12:52,973 --> 00:12:54,173
So you have to lose muscle?

305
00:12:54,503 --> 00:12:55,542
I build muscle really easily.

306
00:12:55,543 --> 00:12:57,543
I know. You build muscle easily.

307
00:12:58,373 --> 00:13:01,442
(He naturally carries her purse.)

308
00:13:01,443 --> 00:13:04,112
So my managers carry it for me.

309
00:13:04,113 --> 00:13:05,153
(Seo Jin carries everything without saying anything.)

310
00:13:06,153 --> 00:13:08,352
You're older now. Do you still build muscle easily?

311
00:13:08,353 --> 00:13:09,992
Yes. It's just how I'm built.

312
00:13:09,993 --> 00:13:13,193
Right. I knew you were like that, but...

313
00:13:13,823 --> 00:13:15,062
I didn't know you were still like that.

314
00:13:15,063 --> 00:13:16,293
- I'm still like that.
- I envy you.

315
00:13:17,063 --> 00:13:18,863
We lost muscle so easily now.

316
00:13:19,263 --> 00:13:21,663
(Mr. Officer has been getting weaker for 23 years.)

317
00:13:21,903 --> 00:13:23,002
(My Star's real manager will go home now.)

318
00:13:23,003 --> 00:13:24,633
- We should do that.
- I'll get going now.

319
00:13:25,103 --> 00:13:27,042
You went through a lot.

320
00:13:27,043 --> 00:13:28,542
- Thank you.
- "You went through a lot?"

321
00:13:28,543 --> 00:13:29,643
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

322
00:13:29,713 --> 00:13:31,142
Why? Is it because there are so many things to carry?

323
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:32,842
- No.
- Am I carrying too much stuff?

324
00:13:32,843 --> 00:13:34,512
- Is it a lot?
- Of everyone so far,

325
00:13:34,513 --> 00:13:35,613
you're carrying the most stuff.

326
00:13:35,713 --> 00:13:36,853
- Is that so?
- Yes.

327
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:38,382
- I don't carry a lot of things.
- You?

328
00:13:38,383 --> 00:13:40,352
We're going abroad.

329
00:13:40,353 --> 00:13:42,653
- That's why.
- I think...

330
00:13:42,723 --> 00:13:45,153
she packs this much even for domestic trips.

331
00:13:46,023 --> 00:13:47,162
- Right? Yes.
- Me?

332
00:13:47,163 --> 00:13:49,292
All actresses carry this much stuff around.

333
00:13:49,293 --> 00:13:51,593
(I think this is pretty standard for actresses.)

334
00:13:52,903 --> 00:13:54,863
You're suddenly taking her side.

335
00:13:56,503 --> 00:13:59,303
I mean, can't you put yourself in an actress' shoes?

336
00:13:59,573 --> 00:14:00,972
Right.

337
00:14:00,973 --> 00:14:02,212
My gosh.

338
00:14:02,213 --> 00:14:04,872
- You're so sweet today.
- Goodness.

339
00:14:04,873 --> 00:14:07,412
You're going to film "Damo" again today.

340
00:14:07,413 --> 00:14:09,652
(There's a sweet vibe between them from the start.)

341
00:14:09,653 --> 00:14:10,852
Do it for us.

342
00:14:10,853 --> 00:14:12,653
- Do what?
- "Does it hurt?"

343
00:14:12,923 --> 00:14:15,393
- No.
- Say, "Does it hurt?"

344
00:14:16,953 --> 00:14:18,992
Is this your first overseas trip with the show?

345
00:14:18,993 --> 00:14:20,422
- It's our 1st time.
- Your 1st overseas trip?

346
00:14:20,423 --> 00:14:21,623
We wouldn't have gone if it hadn't been for you.

347
00:14:23,363 --> 00:14:25,463
- We got to go thanks to you.
- Oh, my.

348
00:14:26,333 --> 00:14:28,002
(Oh, right!)

349
00:14:28,003 --> 00:14:29,303
- Really?
- Would you like some snacks?

350
00:14:29,973 --> 00:14:31,773
Seo Jin brought snacks?

351
00:14:32,043 --> 00:14:33,072
Really?

352
00:14:33,073 --> 00:14:36,013
It's November, and we celebrate Pepero Day.

353
00:14:36,813 --> 00:14:37,813
Here.

354
00:14:37,814 --> 00:14:39,212
(He sweetly gifts her some snacks.)

355
00:14:39,213 --> 00:14:42,782
This one's been discontinued. This is the new premium Pepero.

356
00:14:42,783 --> 00:14:45,212
It looks a lot fancier than the Pepero I know.

357
00:14:45,213 --> 00:14:47,382
- Right?
- It's like a limited edition.

358
00:14:47,383 --> 00:14:49,552
- Yes. Isn't it a limited edition?
- It is a limited edition.

359
00:14:49,553 --> 00:14:50,693
- Is that so?
- It's a limited edition.

360
00:14:51,023 --> 00:14:53,622
- What flavor is this?
- Doesn't it look fancy?

361
00:14:53,623 --> 00:14:54,862
Milk chocolate.

362
00:14:54,863 --> 00:14:55,932
(Sweet vanilla milk chocolate)

363
00:14:55,933 --> 00:14:57,333
You haven't met for a long time,

364
00:14:57,933 --> 00:14:59,602
so Mr. Officer...

365
00:14:59,603 --> 00:15:01,263
- takes good care of you.
- It looks delicious.

366
00:15:03,973 --> 00:15:06,303
I actually eat this often.

367
00:15:06,343 --> 00:15:07,403
You do?

368
00:15:09,713 --> 00:15:11,843
When will I ever get to play the Pepero Game?

369
00:15:14,183 --> 00:15:15,482
Are you saying...

370
00:15:15,483 --> 00:15:16,752
- you want to play it with Ji Won?
- What's the Pepero Game?

371
00:15:16,753 --> 00:15:18,183
Do you want to play the game with her?

372
00:15:18,353 --> 00:15:21,153
No. I was just saying. I could do it with you.

373
00:15:24,623 --> 00:15:25,863
I'm going to spit this out at you.

374
00:15:27,223 --> 00:15:29,132
(I'm picky about who I play with too.)

375
00:15:29,133 --> 00:15:30,192
That's so...

376
00:15:30,193 --> 00:15:32,133
Give it to her and say, "Does it hurt?"

377
00:15:33,003 --> 00:15:35,233
I can't do that so easily.

378
00:15:35,633 --> 00:15:37,633
Read the room.

379
00:15:39,203 --> 00:15:41,073
Read the room.

380
00:15:41,773 --> 00:15:42,913
Does it hurt?

381
00:15:44,273 --> 00:15:45,273
Does it hurt?

382
00:15:45,883 --> 00:15:47,243
It hurts me too.

383
00:15:48,713 --> 00:15:51,653
(He playfully gives the iconic lines with his own twist.)

384
00:15:53,023 --> 00:15:55,223
After our first day of filming,

385
00:15:55,653 --> 00:15:57,023
we got stranded in the mountains...

386
00:15:57,553 --> 00:15:59,823
- because of heavy snowfall, right?
- Yes.

387
00:16:00,323 --> 00:16:03,233
- In Daegwallyeong.
- That was our first day.

388
00:16:04,133 --> 00:16:06,132
And we were all stuck there. Filming was over,

389
00:16:06,133 --> 00:16:07,133
- Right.
- but we couldn't get in our cars...

390
00:16:07,133 --> 00:16:08,133
because it had snowed so much.

391
00:16:09,503 --> 00:16:11,332
There was a cabin.

392
00:16:11,333 --> 00:16:14,303
Ji Won was already there, and I went there too.

393
00:16:14,873 --> 00:16:16,743
She was eating with the staff members.

394
00:16:17,413 --> 00:16:19,083
When I entered the cafeteria,

395
00:16:19,843 --> 00:16:21,513
you were drinking soju.

396
00:16:22,883 --> 00:16:24,483
You were drinking soju.

397
00:16:27,723 --> 00:16:28,852
- You should protect her.
- It...

398
00:16:28,853 --> 00:16:32,323
It was our first day, so we weren't that close.

399
00:16:32,963 --> 00:16:34,692
You were having a glass of soju...

400
00:16:34,693 --> 00:16:35,832
(A glass of soju)

401
00:16:35,833 --> 00:16:38,732
with food.

402
00:16:38,733 --> 00:16:39,833
I thought...

403
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:43,903
you seemed to have a lot of pent-up frustration.

404
00:16:43,973 --> 00:16:45,503
- Really?
- Yes. Somehow...

405
00:16:46,043 --> 00:16:47,043
Really?

406
00:16:47,044 --> 00:16:49,912
(Did I seem like that?)

407
00:16:49,913 --> 00:16:51,812
Yes. Somehow,

408
00:16:51,813 --> 00:16:55,313
it seemed you'd been through a lot.

409
00:16:55,583 --> 00:16:57,353
Having a glass of soju like this.

410
00:16:58,483 --> 00:17:00,182
- She was in her mid-20s.
- She was in her 20s.

411
00:17:00,183 --> 00:17:01,452
No. I was 23.

412
00:17:01,453 --> 00:17:02,692
Exactly. You were in your early 20s.

413
00:17:02,693 --> 00:17:03,752
(She was 25 back then.)

414
00:17:03,753 --> 00:17:05,193
- It was because...
- I was surprised.

415
00:17:05,423 --> 00:17:07,062
I drank soju...

416
00:17:07,063 --> 00:17:09,962
- because I was freezing.
- It was because it was cold?

417
00:17:09,963 --> 00:17:12,332
I drank to warm myself up.

418
00:17:12,333 --> 00:17:15,433
I was too young to enjoy drinking.

419
00:17:15,973 --> 00:17:17,472
You made quite an impression on me back then.

420
00:17:17,473 --> 00:17:20,142
(My Star's first impression was quite something.)

421
00:17:20,143 --> 00:17:22,472
- Really?
- "Does she like drinking?"

422
00:17:22,473 --> 00:17:23,773
I don't even remember.

423
00:17:24,113 --> 00:17:25,842
It left a strong impression on me.

424
00:17:25,843 --> 00:17:27,643
(After 23 years, they realize they have different memories.)

425
00:17:28,613 --> 00:17:29,782
- Hello.
- Hello.

426
00:17:29,783 --> 00:17:31,482
- Shall we sit here?
- Here?

427
00:17:31,483 --> 00:17:32,552
Yes.

428
00:17:32,553 --> 00:17:34,952
We've already used the priority card.

429
00:17:34,953 --> 00:17:36,622
- Do you want to put it here?
- I'll put it here.

430
00:17:36,623 --> 00:17:38,793
(She often loses her phone or bag, so keep an eye on her belongings.)

431
00:17:39,123 --> 00:17:40,522
Gosh, I built muscle.

432
00:17:40,523 --> 00:17:41,822
(Making a big deal)

433
00:17:41,823 --> 00:17:42,833
Gosh.

434
00:17:43,393 --> 00:17:45,332
I want to change my shoes.

435
00:17:45,333 --> 00:17:46,402
- Now?
- My shoes.

436
00:17:46,403 --> 00:17:48,103
Yes. These are too high.

437
00:17:49,273 --> 00:17:50,502
(Looking around)

438
00:17:50,503 --> 00:17:53,373
Ji Won, would you like to have a glass of wine?

439
00:17:54,303 --> 00:17:56,072
- I'll have champagne.
- Champagne?

440
00:17:56,073 --> 00:17:57,212
(I'll have champagne.)

441
00:17:57,213 --> 00:17:59,642
Since it's been so long, let's have our first drink together.

442
00:17:59,643 --> 00:18:00,812
(Are they celebrating their reunion?)

443
00:18:00,813 --> 00:18:02,913
I guess you haven't even eaten together since the drama ended.

444
00:18:04,713 --> 00:18:05,823
Thank you.

445
00:18:07,883 --> 00:18:10,593
(Thanks to Kwang Kyu, she's all set for the long flight.)

446
00:18:11,353 --> 00:18:14,062
- Thank you.
- He's bringing champagne.

447
00:18:14,063 --> 00:18:15,632
(Seo Jin brings over the champagne.)

448
00:18:15,633 --> 00:18:16,963
Ta-da.

449
00:18:17,163 --> 00:18:18,493
It's a party.

450
00:18:20,903 --> 00:18:22,472
(Seo Jin smiles more than usual.)

451
00:18:22,473 --> 00:18:23,703
Cheers.

452
00:18:24,303 --> 00:18:25,702
It's good to see you again.

453
00:18:25,703 --> 00:18:26,802
(For their first overseas business trip)

454
00:18:26,803 --> 00:18:29,413
- It's been a long time.
- My Genie Secretary in Singapore.

455
00:18:30,813 --> 00:18:33,313
(Savoring)

456
00:18:33,483 --> 00:18:35,083
(Exclaiming)

457
00:18:35,413 --> 00:18:36,482
Nice.

458
00:18:36,483 --> 00:18:38,452
(They have a good feeling from the start.)

459
00:18:38,453 --> 00:18:39,582
There aren't a lot of people here.

460
00:18:39,583 --> 00:18:40,722
- This is great.
- This is great.

461
00:18:40,723 --> 00:18:41,882
(The perfect start to their journey)

462
00:18:41,883 --> 00:18:42,992
Is this Singapore Airlines'...

463
00:18:42,993 --> 00:18:44,052
- exclusive lounge?
- Yes.

464
00:18:44,053 --> 00:18:45,222
(A spacious and comfortable private lounge)

465
00:18:45,223 --> 00:18:46,663
- Is this an exclusive lounge?
- Yes.

466
00:18:47,023 --> 00:18:50,563
Singapore Airlines was named the World's Best Airline in 2026.

467
00:18:51,493 --> 00:18:52,533
The World's Best Airline.

468
00:18:53,203 --> 00:18:54,203
Is it that good?

469
00:18:54,204 --> 00:18:56,003
We're like this.

470
00:18:56,303 --> 00:18:59,973
When we're at the office together, we speak casually to each other.

471
00:19:00,703 --> 00:19:03,243
But on set, we use formal language.

472
00:19:03,473 --> 00:19:06,582
Since we're traveling abroad now, call him Mr. Kim.

473
00:19:06,583 --> 00:19:07,913
- Mr. Kim?
- Yes.

474
00:19:08,113 --> 00:19:09,152
Right?

475
00:19:09,153 --> 00:19:10,153
(Laughing)

476
00:19:10,154 --> 00:19:11,213
Mr. Lee?

477
00:19:11,483 --> 00:19:13,082
I'm not your equal.

478
00:19:13,083 --> 00:19:15,052
Call me Captain.

479
00:19:15,053 --> 00:19:17,023
(Call me Captain.)

480
00:19:18,393 --> 00:19:21,323
Why should I call you Captain? My goodness.

481
00:19:21,793 --> 00:19:22,893
- You're unbelievable.
- You...

482
00:19:23,493 --> 00:19:25,962
(Embarrassed)

483
00:19:25,963 --> 00:19:28,403
Wake up. You're not filming "Damo" now.

484
00:19:29,803 --> 00:19:30,872
You still think you're an officer.

485
00:19:30,873 --> 00:19:33,373
(He'll forever be My Star's officer.)

486
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:36,672
By the way, have you guys seen F1?

487
00:19:36,673 --> 00:19:38,342
- No, I haven't.
- Not even once?

488
00:19:38,343 --> 00:19:40,382
- I just saw it on the news.
- Have you not watched the movie?

489
00:19:40,383 --> 00:19:42,313
I watched a documentary yesterday.

490
00:19:42,483 --> 00:19:45,452
It looked so dangerous to me.

491
00:19:45,453 --> 00:19:46,883
- Right.
- Yes.

492
00:19:47,383 --> 00:19:49,223
They must go around 300km per hour in F1.

493
00:19:49,623 --> 00:19:51,393
- It's actually over 350km per hour.
- Right.

494
00:19:52,963 --> 00:19:55,792
(High-speed racing at over 350km per hour)

495
00:19:55,793 --> 00:19:59,003
How on earth do they take those corners?

496
00:19:59,663 --> 00:20:01,063
The tires are really wide.

497
00:20:01,933 --> 00:20:04,602
They have no tread, so they can slide around easily.

498
00:20:04,603 --> 00:20:05,672
(They use slick tires, which have no tread.)

499
00:20:05,673 --> 00:20:07,942
They have no tread. It's just rubber.

500
00:20:07,943 --> 00:20:09,513
They're almost perfectly smooth.

501
00:20:09,913 --> 00:20:12,442
- That's crazy.
- Even a little water...

502
00:20:12,443 --> 00:20:13,813
can make the car spin out.

503
00:20:15,213 --> 00:20:17,783
The tires wear out quickly.

504
00:20:18,313 --> 00:20:20,082
That's why they have to come into the pits...

505
00:20:20,083 --> 00:20:21,923
and change those hot tires in just a few seconds.

506
00:20:22,393 --> 00:20:23,623
The tires can't withstand...

507
00:20:24,153 --> 00:20:25,993
driving at over 300km per hour for hours.

508
00:20:26,293 --> 00:20:27,622
I think those are pretty cool too.

509
00:20:27,623 --> 00:20:29,332
Are they pit boxes?

510
00:20:29,333 --> 00:20:30,832
(It's each team's designated area where the cars stop for servicing.)

511
00:20:30,833 --> 00:20:33,163
- They change tires and stuff.
- Yes.

512
00:20:33,433 --> 00:20:36,372
They change them so quickly, right?

513
00:20:36,373 --> 00:20:38,073
Isn't it sexy?

514
00:20:40,543 --> 00:20:43,343
