01:02:33,053 --> 01:02:34,182
Seo Jin.

1559
01:02:34,183 --> 01:02:36,082
It's so fast, I barely saw it.

1560
01:02:36,083 --> 01:02:37,153
It's super fast.

1561
01:02:39,693 --> 01:02:41,052
Oh, there it is.

1562
01:02:41,053 --> 01:02:43,593
It's so fast. That's crazy.

1563
01:02:44,263 --> 01:02:46,063
That's not the F1 car.

1564
01:02:46,733 --> 01:02:48,233
That's not the F1 car.

1565
01:02:49,233 --> 01:02:51,033
F1 cars are way louder.

1566
01:02:52,073 --> 01:02:54,233
Have you seen it before?

1567
01:02:54,333 --> 01:02:55,802
No.

1568
01:02:55,803 --> 01:02:57,503
- But it's louder.
- No?

1569
01:02:57,703 --> 01:02:59,842
You can hear it.

1570
01:02:59,843 --> 01:03:00,843
Really?

1571
01:03:00,844 --> 01:03:02,082
I've never heard...

1572
01:03:02,083 --> 01:03:03,312
- such a big noise before.
- No.

1573
01:03:03,313 --> 01:03:06,212
- That's not the F1 car sound.
- How do you know that?

1574
01:03:06,213 --> 01:03:07,712
What's that sound then?

1575
01:03:07,713 --> 01:03:10,123
It sounds cheap.

1576
01:03:10,283 --> 01:03:11,823
That's not the F1 car.

1577
01:03:11,953 --> 01:03:13,452
What's that sound then?

1578
01:03:13,453 --> 01:03:14,863
So what is that sound?

1579
01:03:15,493 --> 01:03:17,663
They're just race cars.

1580
01:03:17,723 --> 01:03:19,463
- That's a different race.
- Right, that's a different race.

1581
01:03:20,963 --> 01:03:22,332
It's not the F1.

1582
01:03:22,333 --> 01:03:23,632
He's right. It's not F1.

1583
01:03:23,633 --> 01:03:25,432
They're sports cars like Porsche.

1584
01:03:25,433 --> 01:03:27,803
(Porsche Arbox Carrera Cup Asia before the main F1 games)

1585
01:03:28,343 --> 01:03:29,972
- There they are. In front of us.
- What?

1586
01:03:29,973 --> 01:03:31,002
(Where?)

1587
01:03:31,003 --> 01:03:32,273
I see the sports cars passing by.

1588
01:03:32,413 --> 01:03:33,542
That's crazy.

1589
01:03:33,543 --> 01:03:34,912
That's crazy.

1590
01:03:34,913 --> 01:03:36,543
That's insane.

1591
01:03:37,143 --> 01:03:39,112
He said it's way louder.

1592
01:03:39,113 --> 01:03:40,813
But they all sounded the same.

1593
01:03:41,623 --> 01:03:42,983
Didn't they sound the same?

1594
01:03:43,283 --> 01:03:44,523
They sounded the same.

1595
01:03:45,123 --> 01:03:47,893
Seo Jin doesn't know it either.

1596
01:03:47,923 --> 01:03:49,423
He's just pretending.

1597
01:03:49,793 --> 01:03:51,562
He has bad hearing.

1598
01:03:51,563 --> 01:03:53,433
That's nothing compared to F1.

1599
01:03:54,393 --> 01:03:55,463
(Whirring)

1600
01:03:56,163 --> 01:03:57,232
It's so loud.

1601
01:03:57,233 --> 01:03:58,703
That sound...

1602
01:03:58,773 --> 01:04:00,502
Gosh, that's so loud.

1603
01:04:00,503 --> 01:04:01,742
(The roar of the race cars ringing in their ears)

1604
01:04:01,743 --> 01:04:03,272
That's crazy.

1605
01:04:03,273 --> 01:04:05,413
If it's louder than that,

1606
01:04:05,943 --> 01:04:07,312
we'll need something in our ears.

1607
01:04:07,313 --> 01:04:09,142
That's why, but you...

1608
01:04:09,143 --> 01:04:10,543
You can barely hear anyway. So you'll be fine.

1609
01:04:11,213 --> 01:04:12,483
But...

1610
01:04:13,813 --> 01:04:16,722
There are many people who wear earplugs.

1611
01:04:16,723 --> 01:04:18,752
- What?
- Many do wear earplugs.

1612
01:04:18,753 --> 01:04:21,423
Obviously, if the sound were louder than this.

1613
01:04:22,423 --> 01:04:24,823
It wasn't loud enough to need earplugs.

1614
01:04:25,333 --> 01:04:27,463
The car passes by before you can even put them in.

1615
01:04:27,593 --> 01:04:29,663
"Swoosh!" It's already gone.

1616
01:04:30,863 --> 01:04:33,873
Seriously, it's only a split second. It passes by like, "Swoosh!"

1617
01:04:34,033 --> 01:04:36,473
Swoosh!

1618
01:04:37,073 --> 01:04:39,542
That's why you don't need earplugs.

1619
01:04:39,543 --> 01:04:40,673
(Seo Genie exaggerates.)

1620
01:04:41,683 --> 01:04:43,683
That must be where we're headed.

1621
01:04:44,683 --> 01:04:46,412
(Right next to the Singapore Flyer)

1622
01:04:46,413 --> 01:04:48,852
You mean the place with the tent, right?

1623
01:04:48,853 --> 01:04:51,183
So we'll be watching from up there.

1624
01:04:51,523 --> 01:04:53,492
We're slowly getting closer.

1625
01:04:53,493 --> 01:04:55,523
(Getting excited)

1626
01:04:56,763 --> 01:05:01,333
(A first look inside F1 on Korean television is coming up!)

1627
01:05:02,463 --> 01:05:07,503
(Strict security and safety checks are required before entry.)

1628
01:05:08,133 --> 01:05:09,973
(Amazed)

1629
01:05:11,543 --> 01:05:15,413
(Crowded)

1630
01:05:16,043 --> 01:05:18,353
Just look at the number of people.

1631
01:05:18,753 --> 01:05:20,383
How many have come from all over the world?

1632
01:05:23,023 --> 01:05:27,123
(The F1 venue is packed shoulder to shoulder.)

1633
01:05:28,423 --> 01:05:34,033
(Singapore F1 drew over 300,000 spectators across 3 days.)

1634
01:05:34,663 --> 01:05:36,762
(The place My Star has always dreamed of visiting)

1635
01:05:36,763 --> 01:05:38,203
It feels like a dream.

1636
01:05:38,573 --> 01:05:42,473
The sounds. The energy I could feel at the venue.

1637
01:05:42,843 --> 01:05:45,442
Everything was overwhelming.

1638
01:05:45,443 --> 01:05:46,573
I was on cloud nine.

1639
01:05:47,543 --> 01:05:50,613
(Getting emotional)

1640
01:05:50,883 --> 01:05:53,583
(Where's Kwang Kyu?)

1641
01:05:53,783 --> 01:05:56,353
Why is Kwang Kyu always late?

1642
01:05:56,983 --> 01:05:58,253
Why?

1643
01:05:58,893 --> 01:06:01,592
Why does he always get stopped and come late?

1644
01:06:01,593 --> 01:06:02,623
(In charge of trials and tribulations)

1645
01:06:03,393 --> 01:06:05,993
She's even scanning his legs.

1646
01:06:06,733 --> 01:06:08,762
Kwang Kyu must be hiding something in his pants.

1647
01:06:08,763 --> 01:06:09,933
(Searched from head to toe like a suspected smuggler)

1648
01:06:10,563 --> 01:06:12,403
(Okay?)

1649
01:06:12,903 --> 01:06:16,343
(She still seems suspicious of Kwang Kyu.)

1650
01:06:17,473 --> 01:06:21,113
(Uneasy)

1651
01:06:21,273 --> 01:06:23,143
- Only you got a body scan.
- Why did you...

1652
01:06:23,213 --> 01:06:24,842
Even though she gave me the okay sign...

1653
01:06:24,843 --> 01:06:27,013
(Still feeling uneasy)

1654
01:06:27,853 --> 01:06:31,053
(Off they go again with Kwang Kyu, who has the face of a smuggler!)

1655
01:06:31,583 --> 01:06:34,123
(Looking around)

1656
01:06:34,753 --> 01:06:36,193
There are so many people.

1657
01:06:38,963 --> 01:06:44,003
(More than just a race, F1 is a festival.)

1658
01:06:45,103 --> 01:06:47,333
F1 sure is amazing.

1659
01:06:47,573 --> 01:06:49,043
- Goodness.
- For real.

1660
01:06:50,203 --> 01:06:51,942
People keep talking about F1.

1661
01:06:51,943 --> 01:06:54,373
Some people really do.

1662
01:06:54,613 --> 01:06:57,383
When F1 is held in the US,

1663
01:06:58,113 --> 01:07:00,213
every celebrity you can think of attends.

1664
01:07:00,883 --> 01:07:03,523
(What makes F1 such a special sport?)

1665
01:07:04,183 --> 01:07:07,423
(It's more than a contest between drivers.)

1666
01:07:08,523 --> 01:07:09,962
(Racing machines built with...)

1667
01:07:09,963 --> 01:07:12,163
(staggering investment and cutting-edge technology)

1668
01:07:12,733 --> 01:07:14,392
(An extreme battle...)

1669
01:07:14,393 --> 01:07:17,632
(where drivers put their lives on the line...)

1670
01:07:17,633 --> 01:07:19,633
(at every race, every corner)

1671
01:07:20,103 --> 01:07:23,973
There must be a reason countries around the world pour billions...

1672
01:07:24,673 --> 01:07:26,173
of dollars into hosting F1 races.

1673
01:07:26,643 --> 01:07:28,483
It's like one huge festival.

1674
01:07:30,113 --> 01:07:31,513
(Glancing)

1675
01:07:32,153 --> 01:07:34,413
(Guiding My Star through so she doesn't get lost)

1676
01:07:35,053 --> 01:07:38,493
(Seo Jin leads them to an unusual gate.)

1677
01:07:39,393 --> 01:07:42,762
Yes, please show your wristband for reentry. Thank you so much.

1678
01:07:42,763 --> 01:07:44,022
(They enter after putting on another wristband.)

1679
01:07:44,023 --> 01:07:46,963
Welcome. Make sure you have your wristband.

1680
01:07:49,233 --> 01:07:50,902
(A hidden passage...)

1681
01:07:50,903 --> 01:07:53,972
(opens.)

1682
01:07:53,973 --> 01:07:55,143
What's this?

1683
01:07:56,073 --> 01:07:57,202
What's going on?

1684
01:07:57,203 --> 01:07:58,343
- It's like a sauna.
- Is this an elevator?

1685
01:07:58,613 --> 01:07:59,743
Are we in an elevator?

1686
01:08:00,243 --> 01:08:01,612
It's an elevator.

1687
01:08:01,613 --> 01:08:02,643
(An elevator to a lounge with a prime view of F1)

1688
01:08:03,143 --> 01:08:04,243
Interesting.

1689
01:08:06,313 --> 01:08:08,723
(Curious)

1690
01:08:09,583 --> 01:08:11,853
(Are even the elevators different at F1?)

1691
01:08:16,623 --> 01:08:18,833
(Her eyes are sparkling.)

1692
01:08:21,263 --> 01:08:23,103
Does the elevator go extra fast on purpose?

1693
01:08:23,203 --> 01:08:24,862
- No way.
- No?

1694
01:08:24,863 --> 01:08:26,802
It'll be dismantled after the event.

1695
01:08:26,803 --> 01:08:28,403
(To be dismantled after the event)

1696
01:08:28,543 --> 01:08:29,572
- Sorry.
- The exit must be...

1697
01:08:29,573 --> 01:08:30,602
on the other side.

1698
01:08:30,603 --> 01:08:33,273
(They arrive at the prime viewing floor.)

1699
01:08:35,883 --> 01:08:36,943
This way.

1700
01:08:37,543 --> 01:08:38,613
Thank you.

1701
01:08:39,213 --> 01:08:40,512
- What?
- What's this?

1702
01:08:40,513 --> 01:08:41,652
(Stepping out, full of anticipation)

1703
01:08:41,653 --> 01:08:42,753
Where do we go?

1704
01:08:43,283 --> 01:08:45,222
Vanda Suite. It's our suite.

1705
01:08:45,223 --> 01:08:46,553
(Vanda Suite?)

1706
01:08:47,153 --> 01:08:48,823
Vanda Suite?

1707
01:08:49,223 --> 01:08:50,223
Is it here?

1708
01:08:50,223 --> 01:08:51,223
(Vanda Suite: A hospitality lounge for the guests...)

1709
01:08:51,224 --> 01:08:52,493
(of the Singapore Tourism Board)

1710
01:08:53,433 --> 01:08:55,833
- Hi.
- Hi. Welcome to Vanda Suite.

1711
01:08:56,163 --> 01:08:57,662
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

1712
01:08:57,663 --> 01:08:59,302
- Hi, welcome.
- Thank you.

1713
01:08:59,303 --> 01:09:01,873
(An exclusive space for the Singapore Tourism Board invitees)

1714
01:09:03,403 --> 01:09:05,002
- Here?
- Yes.

1715
01:09:05,003 --> 01:09:06,013
(Amazed)

1716
01:09:08,013 --> 01:09:09,243
Oh, my gosh.

1717
01:09:10,683 --> 01:09:12,652
(The racetrack unfolds right before their eyes.)

1718
01:09:12,653 --> 01:09:13,813
Unbelievable.

1719
01:09:16,623 --> 01:09:19,823
(A view of double apex corners)

1720
01:09:19,923 --> 01:09:22,993
(A prime spot to watch drivers battle for overtakes)

1721
01:09:23,723 --> 01:09:28,033
(Now this is a lounge worthy of My Star.)

1722
01:09:28,163 --> 01:09:31,933
(Even the usually practical Seo Jin admires the track, eyes sparkling.)

1723
01:09:33,903 --> 01:09:36,703
(How does this lounge compare with other ticket options?)

1724
01:09:37,703 --> 01:09:39,842
(General admission: Around 550 to 730 dollars)

1725
01:09:39,843 --> 01:09:40,843
(No assigned seating.)

1726
01:09:40,844 --> 01:09:42,043
(You watch the race standing outdoors near the trackside fence.)

1727
01:09:42,813 --> 01:09:45,042
(Reserved grandstand seating: Around 600 to 2,500 dollars)

1728
01:09:45,043 --> 01:09:46,753
(Assigned outdoor seats overlooking key corners and straightaways)

1729
01:09:48,683 --> 01:09:51,352
(Indoor VIP hospitality: Around 5,000 to 15,000 dollars)

1730
01:09:51,353 --> 01:09:54,123
(Air-conditioned indoor areas with buffet dining and an open bar)

1731
01:09:54,353 --> 01:09:56,322
(A quick guide to F1 ticket tiers, based on 3-day passes)

1732
01:09:56,323 --> 01:10:00,033
(These tickets are available to anyone who can afford them.)

1733
01:10:00,793 --> 01:10:03,462
(But this lounge is invitation-only!)

1734
01:10:03,463 --> 01:10:06,003
- Let's go outside.
- We can go outside.

1735
01:10:06,133 --> 01:10:07,272
You can watch it outside.

1736
01:10:07,273 --> 01:10:08,573
- Really?
- Yes.

1737
01:10:12,043 --> 01:10:15,243
(This is truly awesome.)

1738
01:10:17,013 --> 01:10:18,112
I'm loving it.

1739
01:10:18,113 --> 01:10:19,113
(Taking in the atmosphere firsthand)

1740
01:10:19,813 --> 01:10:21,553
They must be getting ready.

1741
01:10:21,983 --> 01:10:23,552
- They must be getting ready.
- What?

1742
01:10:23,553 --> 01:10:25,422
Which is your good side, Ji Won?

1743
01:10:25,423 --> 01:10:27,692
- This side.
- The left? Okay.

1744
01:10:27,693 --> 01:10:29,663
(Taking promotional photos for the Singapore Tourism Board)

1745
01:10:30,393 --> 01:10:33,463
(My Star has arrived at Singapore F1!)

1746
01:10:33,633 --> 01:10:34,662
(I'm also excited!)

1747
01:10:34,663 --> 01:10:37,103
Kwang Kyu is going all in.

1748
01:10:37,403 --> 01:10:40,172
Look this way for a second. Nice.

1749
01:10:40,173 --> 01:10:42,543
Good. Rock and roll!

1750
01:10:43,403 --> 01:10:45,372
(My Star takes over the Singapore Tourism Board's social media.)

1751
01:10:45,373 --> 01:10:46,873
Yes, My Star.

1752
01:10:47,513 --> 01:10:48,783
We'll let her put those cups.

1753
01:10:49,143 --> 01:10:52,382
(A short break in the lounge before the race)

1754
01:10:52,383 --> 01:10:53,713
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1755
01:10:54,913 --> 01:10:56,083
What time is it right now?

1756
01:10:57,823 --> 01:10:59,022
There's still some time left.

1757
01:10:59,023 --> 01:11:01,093
(A little time remains before the F1 race.)

1758
01:11:03,323 --> 01:11:05,663
- It's Kimi!
- What?

1759
01:11:06,193 --> 01:11:07,762
- Who?
- Kimi.

1760
01:11:07,763 --> 01:11:09,603
- It's Kimi.
- That's Kimi.

1761
01:11:10,033 --> 01:11:12,432
Aren't we watching him live right now?

1762
01:11:12,433 --> 01:11:13,773
- We are.
- Yes.

1763
01:11:14,133 --> 01:11:15,202
It's live.

1764
01:11:15,203 --> 01:11:17,342
- Kimi!
- It's Kimi.

1765
01:11:17,343 --> 01:11:19,973
(She can't hide her excitement at the sight of Kimi.)

1766
01:11:20,173 --> 01:11:22,043
Help me meet him.

1767
01:11:23,683 --> 01:11:25,243
Help me, okay?

1768
01:11:26,913 --> 01:11:29,153
- He will, right?
- Yes, Seo Jin will definitely help.

1769
01:11:30,083 --> 01:11:32,553
- After all, he's from New York.
- Exactly.

1770
01:11:33,353 --> 01:11:35,223
(Feeling massive pressure)

1771
01:11:35,393 --> 01:11:38,323
So I have an ultimate goal I want to achieve this time.

1772
01:11:38,663 --> 01:11:40,133
- It's...
- Is it to meet Max?

1773
01:11:40,463 --> 01:11:41,533
Yes.

1774
01:11:41,763 --> 01:11:43,033
Help me meet them.

1775
01:11:43,203 --> 01:11:44,403
(She's desperate.)

1776
01:11:44,603 --> 01:11:47,172
I'll get you to meet them, even if I get run over!

1777
01:11:47,173 --> 01:11:50,803
(I'll get you to meet them, even if I get run over!)

1778
01:11:53,413 --> 01:11:54,842
(Mr. Officer is risking his life for My Star.)

1779
01:11:54,843 --> 01:11:56,482
- You're really amazing.
- That's so cool.

1780
01:11:56,483 --> 01:11:57,513
That's so cool.

1781
01:11:57,913 --> 01:12:00,783
(Gosh, I made a promise.)

1782
01:12:01,783 --> 01:12:02,883
Hello.

1783
01:12:04,053 --> 01:12:06,452
Seo Jin, over there.

1784
01:12:06,453 --> 01:12:07,623
Hello.

1785
01:12:09,393 --> 01:12:11,863
(A man in a suit appears.)

1786
01:12:12,433 --> 01:12:15,563
(Instinctively sensing he's someone important)

1787
01:12:16,563 --> 01:12:17,632
(Oliver Chong,)

1788
01:12:17,633 --> 01:12:19,303
(Assistant Chief Executive of the Singapore Tourism Board)

1789
01:12:20,433 --> 01:12:22,743
(The assistant chief executive?)

1790
01:12:23,903 --> 01:12:25,912
- Is it him?
- What?

1791
01:12:25,913 --> 01:12:27,373
- Have you met him before?
- Okay.

1792
01:12:28,573 --> 01:12:30,613
- Hello. Hey.
- Hello.

1793
01:12:30,843 --> 01:12:32,183
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

1794
01:12:32,413 --> 01:12:36,783
- This is Ms. Ha and Mr. Kim.
- Mr. Kim.

1795
01:12:37,653 --> 01:12:38,823
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

1796
01:12:39,493 --> 01:12:41,422
- Ji Won.
- Thank you.

1797
01:12:41,423 --> 01:12:42,463
Ji Won.

1798
01:12:43,563 --> 01:12:45,433
Welcome to Singapore again.

1799
01:12:46,593 --> 01:12:47,892
You visited in January,

1800
01:12:47,893 --> 01:12:49,603
- and now you're back.
- Yes.

1801
01:12:49,703 --> 01:12:51,663
- Thank you.
- I just wanted to say that...

1802
01:12:51,863 --> 01:12:53,403
I really like this picture.

1803
01:12:54,073 --> 01:12:57,042
- Yes. It's my painting.
- It's my favorite.

1804
01:12:57,043 --> 01:12:59,172
It was at an exhibition...

1805
01:12:59,173 --> 01:13:00,842
- Yes.
- which was held in January.

1806
01:13:00,843 --> 01:13:02,013
(It was displayed at an exhibition in Singapore.)

1807
01:13:02,583 --> 01:13:03,642
It's very well done.

1808
01:13:03,643 --> 01:13:04,712
- I really like it.
- Thank you.

1809
01:13:04,713 --> 01:13:06,283
- Thank you so much.
- The color, you know.

1810
01:13:06,553 --> 01:13:08,712
Thank you for inviting me to F1.

1811
01:13:08,713 --> 01:13:11,983
I'm really excited to be here. Thank you so much.

1812
01:13:12,293 --> 01:13:13,692
Just now on the boat,

